WEBVTT

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.970
"Continental Calendar"
"Early November, 1546"

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.230
How is that matter coming along?

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.690
Sire, the plan is making steady progress.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.070
One might even...
say it is going smoothly.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:34.740
That sounds a little evasive. Is there
something we should be worried about?

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.160
It may be going a bit <i>too </i>smoothly.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.290
Almost like there was
some other will at work.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.580
In which case,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.330
it is conceivable that the outcome
could take an unexpected turn.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.630
I'd like to avoid any
unforeseen circumstances,

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.090
but at this point, we can't
exactly back out, either.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.510
No, sire.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.880
We can't alter the plan.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.890
Keep your eyes open for any changes,
and move things forward.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.810
Understood.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.810
Your Majesty!

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.560
What's with the rush?

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.820
A-And Prime Minister,
please excuse my interruption.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.320
So, what's the matter, Ludwin?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:24.410
A-An acquaintance of mine has
done something outrageous!

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.370
Something outrageous?

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.500
<i>"...Keep on going anyway"</i>

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:38.550
<i>Our bond strikes deep into my left breast</i>

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.390
<i>We enjoy a fleeting happiness</i>
<i>after weathering one fog,</i>

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:52.400
<i>until our vision becomes obscured again</i>

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.360
<i>Bitterly betrayed, we grow</i>
<i>disgusted by our destiny</i>

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>But why does the dawn still come?</i>

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.580
<i>We close our eyes and try to remember</i>

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.920
<i>the chance of stopping, of never meeting</i>

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.510
<i>From boundless zero to infinity,</i>

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:25.020
<i>dreaming is the heartbeat of believing</i>

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.850
<i>We'll move along alone and in pairs</i>

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:34.980
<i>Don't stay put; our small,</i>
<i>though by no means helpless steps</i>

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.780
<i>will open uncharted territory</i>
<i>for each of us</i>

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:45.870
<i>Realize we will never again</i>
<i>let our dreams die on the vine</i>

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:52.670
<i>The tear tracks that run down</i>
<i>our cheeks are shooting stars</i>

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.500
<i>We're going to grab hold of them</i>

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.430
"Strike While the Iron is Hot"

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.230
So this person is a childhood
friend of Ludwin's, right?

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:13.770
Yeah, she's been called the
Forbidden Army's mad scientist.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:17.900
The Forbidden Army's... It seems like
I've heard of her somewhere before.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.700
A garage?!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.620
Er, nothing, never mind.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.160
Ludwin, what is this?

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.370
A dungeon entrance, Your Majesty.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.790
Dungeon? You mean like
a "dungeon" dungeon?

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.540
Is it supposed to be so artificial?

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.170
There are many different types.
There are caves,

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:43.090
the basements of fortresses,
paved with stone,

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:46.970
and even mysterious spaces
encased by metal.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.600
And this is an abandoned dungeon,

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.140
bequeathed by the royal family,
turned into a research facility,

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.980
and moved into by the
eccentric Maxwell family.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:01.700
Genia? It's me, Ludwin Arcs.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.490
Genia, are you all right?!

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:10.410
Lu, you called out and startled me,
so I knocked some things over.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:14.250
Whew, I'm just glad there weren't any
dangerous chemicals or anything.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.350
It's metal.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.930
What are you doing?

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:33.600
Huh? The floor is glowing.
You don't think that's strange?

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.940
Must be magic.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.150
It must be because you can
do anything with magic here

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:44.070
that Liscia and the others feel less
than bowled over by all this.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:50.450
This is the lowest level,
where Genia's laboratory is.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.840
Wh-What is this place?!

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.690
Your Majesty...

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.400
This is Genia's laboratory.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:26.150
Okay, I'm coming now, Lu.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.240
Hey, Lu. Thanks for coming.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.120
Who are those two guys?

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:39.750
H-Hey! How rude! This is His Majesty
King Souma and Princess Liscia!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.630
I'm terribly sorry about this,
Your Majesty, Princess!

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.800
Ah, you're right.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:48.930
On closer look, I see your face all
the time on the Gemstone Broadcasts.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:56.560
It is an honor to meet you, Your Majesty.
My name is Genia Maxwell.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:01.190
Souma Kazuya, provisional king
of the Kingdom of Elfrieden.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.980
This is my fiancée...

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.280
Liscia Elfrieden.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:11.490
I am well aware! I humbly proffer you
all good health and every happiness!

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:15.000
You don't have to be so formal with us.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.910
We're the ones who are
dropping in on you, after all.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.130
Just speak casually to us, please.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:23.750
Oh, yeah? Okay, then, you betcha.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.340
G-Genia!

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.260
It's all right.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.840
B-But sire...

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.640
We'll deal with the "outrage"
business later.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:34.430
Right now, I'm more
interested in Genia herself.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:41.600
I hate to stand out here and talk,
so come on in. I'll make us some coffee.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:53.740
Let's start over. I am Genia Maxwell,

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:58.160
researcher, scientist, and inventor.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.080
Oh, I suppose I'm also
a Forbidden Army mage.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.750
I was with the weapons
development division,

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.510
but I did some things
that got me dismissed.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.970
What did you do?

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:11.590
She created something quite scandalous.

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:14.300
You know how war tears up
the countryside, right?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:18.310
Well I made these arrowheads loaded
with seeds for fast-growing plants

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:22.650
so that wherever there was a war,
there would be lots of greenery.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:27.320
Tr-Tree-planting during wartime? That idea
is a bit too far-fetched, isn't it?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.240
I hate to blow my own horn...

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.780
...but I think it was a great idea.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.750
But maybe I shouldn't have had
them enchanted with light magic

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:43.960
to help accelerate the plants' growth.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.590
I remember!

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:50.510
The mad scientist of the Forbidden Army!
That was <i>your </i>doing, wasn't it?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.420
Hmm?

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:55.430
I'm not sure I want to ask,
but what happened?

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:58.970
Well, you see, before
you were summoned here,

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.770
a training ground and
the laboratory attached to it

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.520
were once swallowed up by a sea of trees.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.870
I never expected it to end up
like that all at once.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.040
Uh-huh...

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.790
Genia, don't get started.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:27.590
I didn't like the atmosphere
in the development division.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:32.170
It's weird for everyone to be going
in the same direction, isn't it?

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.340
There should be more
freedom of ideas, right?

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:41.220
I believe that superior inventions
are born of free ideas.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.980
Ludwin, you sure have your
hands full with her, huh?

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.190
Your Majesty!

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:50.730
By the way, King, do you know what
kind of lineage the Maxwells have?

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.240
Oh, their house distinguished
themselves by researching

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:56.160
the artifacts that have been
brought back from dungeons.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:01.370
Yes. My family has been conducting
research for generations.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.960
And after all those years of research,

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.790
we've started to get a vague
glimpse of "something."

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.380
"Something"?

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:13.840
A natural law, separate from magic.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.720
A separate natural law?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.390
King, you use Gemstones a lot, right?

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:23.560
Do you understand what
sort of things those are?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:28.900
Yes, as I understand it, they are ancient
artifacts discovered in dungeons,

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.440
and the magic of the Sylph wind spirits,

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:35.820
and the Undine water spirits are
incorporated within them, right?

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:39.780
That's how they deliver
the picture and sound.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.950
There are two things wrong
with your perception.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.370
Wrong?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:49.380
The first is the part where
the magic of Sylph wind spirits,

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:55.090
and that of the Undine water
spirits are incorporated.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.180
But there <i>are </i>spirits, right?

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:03.640
I-I've never seen one, myself.
Spirits come from the world of mythology.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:08.270
So then, that doesn't
prove their existence.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:14.070
Because of the magic in our world,
the truth becomes harder to see.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.030
Everything that is mysterious
gets categorized

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:23.540
as being the power of magic or spirits.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.750
As a result, there are a lot
of things nobody sees.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.710
The truth is like this, though--

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:33.420
While researching the Gemstones
that were found in the dungeons,

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.550
it was discovered by accident that if you
use water and wind magic on them,

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.050
they took in the view
that was around them,

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:45.850
and projected it to the receivers
that were also discovered with them.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.900
The business about Sylph and Undine magic

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:54.900
is the thinking that maybe it's the grace
of these spirits that makes it possible,

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.240
and is nothing more than an afterthought.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:00.570
So you're saying that
there aren't any spirits?

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:06.080
I can't say that for certain, either.
I mean, it's possible that there are.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.210
And so, the second part you have wrong...

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:18.090
...is the part where the "picture
and sound are delivered."

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.050
N-No, that part's not wrong, is it?

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:26.430
Like I was just saying, the transmitting
functions of the Gemstones

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:30.140
were discovered by accident
while they were being researched.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:35.360
In other words, we're only using
the Gemstones to do broadcasts.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:41.030
Huh? So then, are you saying that's not
what the Gemstones were meant for?

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.330
Then what exactly <i>are </i>the Gemstones?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.790
They're what's known as "dungeon cores."

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.460
Dungeon cores?

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:54.460
Dungeon cores.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:12:00.550
They're said to be the most important
things in supporting a dungeon.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:06.100
As long as they're there, ferocious
monsters will keep appearing.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:10.810
If you destroy it or shut it down,
the monsters stop appearing,

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:13.560
and the dungeon becomes abandoned.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:17.110
Adventurers go out and explore dungeons,

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:22.900
but their ultimate objective is to
shut down the dungeon core.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:25.120
If they bring back a dungeon core,

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:29.790
they are able to earn a huge amount
of wealth and honor from the nation.

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:33.580
Which means, all the things
we call Gemstones now

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:36.210
are destroyed dungeon cores,

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:41.050
and we can only study them
in their broken state right now.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:50.520
Nobody yet has ever brought back
a working dungeon core to the surface.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.640
We can't have more monsters
up here, can we?

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:58.570
Okay, maybe not, but wouldn't you
like to study one that's working

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.980
to find out what they're supposed to be?

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.610
Can't you restart one?

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:09.370
It hasn't been possible so far.
We don't even know how they work.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.830
The unknown is scary.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.170
Which is why people use
magic to explain everything.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.170
What do you mean by that?

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:23.920
People are surprisingly
reasonable creatures.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:28.720
If we can't recognize something
and give it an explanation, we fear it.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.970
So we force explanations on things if we
have to, to try to understand them.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.190
I knew you'd know what I'm talking about!

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.850
I'm glad you understand me, King.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:40.690
Hey, in the world I come from,

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:45.900
we had the pursuit of "science," which
was a different natural law from magic.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:51.080
Oh, yeah? I'd sure like to hear
all about that sometime.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.540
We of the House of Maxwell call
this study of a separate natural law

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.830
"Over-science"

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.830
"over-science" for convenience sake.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.290
"Over-science"

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.290
Over-science?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:05.510
Which makes me an over-scientist.

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:09.890
Now then, I sure would like such
a sure-to-be sympathizing king

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:13.260
to have a look at my inventions.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.860
This is my latest invention!

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.240
The Little Susumu Mark V!

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.040
That name is lame.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:39.500
You know how large-scale ships are
propelled by wind power or sea dragons?

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:45.130
Well, the Little Susumu Mark V
alone can propel a whole ship!

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:48.170
Oh, so it's a propulsion device.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:51.180
Correct! This machine, you see,

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.260
sucks in whatever is in
the space in front of the loop,

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.270
then shoots it out into
the space behind it!

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.850
Hmm? If it sucks in what's
in the space in front of it,

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.400
what happens if you use it
the way it is right now?

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:10.160
Aren't you a sharp one? On land,
it can suck in air, then shoot it out.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.820
Shall we try an experiment?

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.080
Uh, Genia, just a minute!

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:42.770
Your Majesty! Princess!

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:43.730
Are you all right?!

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:44.730
More or less.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:45.690
Still alive.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.400
Sorry, sorry!

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.030
I had it pointing backwards.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:57.040
Genia! What if something had
happened to His Majesty?!

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.370
Now, now, we're fine. It's all right.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:03.210
I have to say, Genia,
this is an amazing invention!

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.330
Isn't it?

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:08.760
This loop part is a special metal that
has a modified spell engraved in it

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:12.300
that allows it to channel energy.

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:16.390
And so, by feeding it energy,
you get this Little Susumu Mark V,

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.930
a machine which takes in
and expels magicium.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:24.980
Just one of these can do
the work of a giant sea dragon.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.570
What's your source of power?
It would have to be magic, right?

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.900
It has one of these installed in it.

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.320
Hmm?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.320
Isn't that curse ore?

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:36.990
You know what it is, Liscia?

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:42.370
You know what? We use magic
to mine ores, too.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:45.750
But whenever this curse ore is nearby,

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.420
our magic stops working for some reason.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.760
And if you try to force it to work...

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:52.920
Ka-boom!

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:55.590
It explodes? That sounds dangerous.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:59.510
If you're digging through a mine
and you run into this ore,

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:02.560
it means you can't mine anything more.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:07.730
That's why it's called curse ore--
stone that is divinely jinxed.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:12.610
And unfortunately, there's a large vein
of it running beneath the kingdom.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:15.570
You shouldn't sound
so ridiculous, Princess.

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:16.240
Huh?

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:20.120
On the contrary, one might say
the fact that there's so much of this

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:23.540
buried beneath the kingdom shows
that we are divinely blessed.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:27.330
Curse ore doesn't prevent us
from using magic.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:31.710
Think about it for a minute. You can't
use magic when near the ore,

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:34.800
and if you try to use it anyway,
it explodes.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.930
So then, where does the energy
for that come from?

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:42.310
Hold on a minute! Are you saying
that curse ore absorbs magic?

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:45.270
Impressive, King! That's right.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:49.230
This ore absorbs the energy of magic.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:54.490
When it exceeds its tolerance level,
it releases that stored energy.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:57.030
Explosively so, in fact.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:04.950
I've succeeded in retrieving the magic
energy absorbed by the curse ore.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:08.920
And, I'm using it as the power
source for this device.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.460
You're what?

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:18.220
This is really serious. If it's true,
it's like a rechargeable battery.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:22.350
Genia has developed the
technology to store energy

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:26.730
here in a world that doesn't
even have the steam engine.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:31.060
With this technology, the kingdom
could make a giant leap forward.

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:39.780
However, once it gets out that
the power source is a cursed stone,

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:44.080
it's bound to create religious
friction in this world.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.250
Moreover, according to Liscia,

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:50.540
there's a major vein of curse
ore within the kingdom.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:54.630
If we don't play this right, there
could be a war over our resources.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:58.380
In other words, not only
could this technology

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:03.220
potentially make us the greatest
power on the continent,

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:07.140
it is also potentially dangerous
enough to destroy the country.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.190
Souma, what's the matter?

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:10.350
Huh?

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:14.400
Oh, sorry. Imagining the high risk,
high reward of this situation

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:16.530
has made me feel out of sorts.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:24.450
Genia just became as critical
to us as Tomoe is.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.330
Huh?

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:28.870
I'll explain in detail later.
More immediately,

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:32.290
what can we do to anchor
Genia here in our country?

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:36.380
I think that her being a member of
the House of Maxwell would be enough.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:40.630
But if I had to say, she could
marry someone that you trust,

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.550
and raise a family here.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:48.520
Yeah, I guess. Do you think
she has any feelings for Ludwin?

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:52.730
Speaking as a fellow woman,
I'd give it a 60% chance.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:55.480
You women are hard to understand.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.190
Then, Souma, what's your take on Ludwin?

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:05.030
Oh, I'm 99% sure he likes her.
Men are easy to read in that regard.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.290
Ludwin, do you like Genia?

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:16.380
H-How can you ask me that
out of the blue, Your Majesty?!

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:19.510
Genia is a key figure for our kingdom.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:23.090
So I want her to be married
to someone I can trust.

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:27.970
You want me to be Lu's wife?

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:31.140
Genia, would you object
to marrying Ludwin?

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.600
Mm-mm, I wouldn't.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:39.650
I always thought that someday
I would settle down with somebody.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:43.660
I've also thought that you would be
a pretty good person for that, Lu.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:50.830
Huh?! B-But Your Majesty, that would mean
the end of the Maxwell family line!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:54.790
Then she can always go by "Maxwell-Arcs."

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:59.500
Ah, and you have my word, the royal
family will pay for the whole wedding.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.420
Are there any other issues to address?

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:05.470
Ludwin, get your nerve up.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:07.050
R-Right!

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:11.930
Would you be my wife?

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:17.940
Are you sure you want me, Lu?
I'm not exactly noblewoman material.

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:22.490
I know. Even so, I want you
at my side from now on.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:24.530
You sure have odd tastes.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:28.830
But mm-hmm, okay. I look
forward to being with you.

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:33.790
I trust that everyone is happy
with this arrangement?

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.670
No, Your Majesty, not yet.

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:40.460
I got caught up by Genia's reaction,
so I forgot to mention something.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:44.590
She's the one who committed
that scandalous act.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:49.890
Oh yeah, that's right, huh? I was so
excited by the new invention, I forgot.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:51.180
Yes...

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:55.060
Ow!

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:59.480
Lu, I won't have any domestic violence
so early in our engagement.

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:03.740
You idiot! Look, you and I are going
to apologize to His Majesty together!

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:09.030
I apologize for what my... fiancée...

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:10.950
...has done. There can be no excuse.

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:13.330
Hey, you're hurting me, Lu!

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:17.370
Uh-huh. So, what is it that she did?

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:21.630
She stole dragon bones.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:24.590
Ow...

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:39.100
<i>"What are we supposed to choose?"</i>

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:44.360
<i>Our voices imploring the future are hoarse</i>

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:50.450
<i>We've become so afraid</i>
<i>of what we could lose</i>

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:55.410
<i>that we're just frozen in place</i>

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:59.870
<i>How many times have we made mistakes</i>

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:05.840
<i>because we wanted to check our "answers"?</i>

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:13.180
<i>Before we knew it we were in love,</i>
<i>we had fallen in love</i>

00:23:13.180 --> 00:23:17.430
<i>I'll hold fast to you</i>
<i>in the times we're in</i>

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:23.230
<i>We who set alight</i>
<i>our finite lives to fight</i>

00:23:23.230 --> 00:23:28.490
<i>are noble and beautiful above all</i>

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:32.450
<i>As long as we create</i>
<i>as many bright tomorrows</i>

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.790
<i>as the indelible wounds we suffer,</i>

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:46.840
<i>we can be proud of all</i>
<i>we've woven together</i>
